     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\">Olá a todos,<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\">Aqui fica uma curiosidade. No outro dia estive a tentar mapear a drive para ver quais os ficheiros que tem maior dimensão.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\">O código ainda precisa de uns valentes toques (aceitam-se contribuições), mas já comecei o caminho ...e aqui fica ele para quem quiser:<br><br>library(treemap)<br>library(tsne)<br><br>df &lt;- <a href=\"http://file.info\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://file.info&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793410999185000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3YLlBQzxeNn_F63qOCLhTM\">file.info</a>(list.files(&quot;.&quot;, all.files = TRUE, recursive=TRUE))[,1:4] #lists all files in the current folder<br>df &lt;- df[!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793410999186000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fT1gXyBRzjVqvaye4AV9M\">is.na</a>(df$size),] # exclude missing rows<br>df$nam &lt;- row.names(df) #add file names col<br>df$name &lt;- gsub( &quot;.*$/&quot;, &quot;&quot;, df$nam)#substr(df$nam,1,4) #get file names - need improvement<br>df$type &lt;- gsub(&quot;^.*?\\\\.&quot;,&quot;&quot;,df$nam) #get file type - need improvement<br>df$lsize &lt;- log10(df$size+1) # a nicer scale<br>summary(df)<br>treemap(df,<br>       index=c(&quot;name&quot;),<br>       vSize=&quot;size&quot;,<br>       vColor=&quot;type&quot;,<br>       palette=&quot;RdBu&quot;)<br><br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\">Abraço e tudo a correr bem,<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\">M.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;color:rgb(19,79,92)\"><br clear=\"all\"></div><br>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"1\"><b style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153);font-family:garamond,serif\">Marta M. Rufino</b><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153);font-family:garamond,serif\"> (</span></font><font size=\"1\"><font size=\"1\"><font color=\"#339999\" face=\"garamond, serif\">Postdoctoral Researcher</font></font></font><font size=\"1\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153);font-family:garamond,serif\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153);font-family:garamond,serif\"></span><b style=\"color:rgb(51,153,153);font-family:garamond,serif\"><i><br>____________________________________________________<br><span style=\"color:rgb(153,51,153)\"></span></i></b></font><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148)\"><font size=\"1\"><span style=\"font-family:garamond,serif\"><b>IPMA</b> (Portuguese Institute for the Sea and Atmosphere)</span></font></span></div><div><font color=\"#134f5c\" face=\"garamond, serif\">Rua Alfredo Magalhães Ramalho, 6<font size=\"1\"><br></font></font></div><div><font color=\"#134f5c\" face=\"garamond, serif\">1495-006 Lisboa<br></font><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:garamond,serif\">Portugal</span></div><div><font color=\"#134f5c\" face=\"garamond, serif\">Telefone: </font><span style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:garamond,serif;font-size:x-small\"><a href=\"tel:+351%2021%20302%207076\" value=\"+351213027076\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(+351) 21 302 7076</a> </span><br></div><div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#134f5c\" face=\"garamond, serif\"><a href=\"http://ipmaescolas.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ipmaescolas.wordpress.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793410999186000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0X-LkdnwE_GhpslgdpFS0L\">Blogue IPMA-Escolas</a>